{
  "kind": "flow-node",
  "version": 2,
  "tool": "arc",
  "meta": {
    "label": "Arc",
    "category": "2d primitives",
    "color": "#ca8a04"
  },
  "description": "A 2D arc (open polyline): centre (x, y), radius, from Start angle to End angle (degrees).",
  "instructions": "Draws a circular arc as an OPEN polyline — centred at (centerX, centerY) in metres, of the given radius, sweeping from Start angle to End angle (degrees, the short way). Every field can be wired from a Math or Math Engine node, so it's ideal for a door swing (centre = hinge, radius = leaf width, Start = closed, End = open). It has no fill.",
